--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

tools/legacy-libs/
    Prebuilt compatibility shared libraries (libtinfo, libncurses, libssl,
    libcrypto) redistributed unmodified from Ubuntu's package archive, so
    that Vivado 2025.1 can run on distributions that no longer ship these
    soname versions. They remain under their own upstream licences
    (ncurses: MIT-style; OpenSSL: Apache-2.0) and are not covered by the
    GPL-2.0 terms above.

docs/img/board.jpg
    Product photograph of the board, from the distributor's own listing.

docs/img/boot-sd-00.jpg, boot-qspi-10.jpg, boot-jtag-11.jpg
    Photographs of the BOOT DIP switch positions, from the distributor's
    PlutoSky R1 write-up:
    https://blog.opensourcesdrlab.com/archives/PlutoSky-R1

firmware/src/  (not committed; fetched by firmware/scripts/setup.sh)
    Linux (GPL-2.0), U-Boot (GPL-2.0+) and Buildroot (mostly MIT/BSD, with
    individual packages under their own licences), from
    https://github.com/Xiaozhang-code-cloud/Fish-Wan-plutosdr-fw-7020-SDR

    The diffs in firmware/patches/ apply to that GPL-2.0 source and are
    distributed under GPL-2.0 accordingly.

    AMD embeddedsw (MIT), from https://github.com/Xilinx/embeddedsw, pinned to
    tag xilinx_v2025.1. The boot loader is compiled from it. The files under
    firmware/fsbl/generated/ are HSI-generated outputs describing this board's
    hardware design and carry embeddedsw's MIT terms.

    AMD bootgen (Apache-2.0), from https://github.com/Xilinx/bootgen, pinned to
    tag xilinx_v2025.1. Built from source by setup.sh and used to package
    BOOT.bin, so that no AMD binary is required.

AMD/Xilinx Vivado and any AMD IP referenced by the HDL projects are
proprietary, licensed separately by AMD, and not covered by this repository.
Vivado is needed only to build the FPGA bitstream; given an already-built
hardware platform (--xsa), nothing from AMD is required at all.
